.TH CHTTPSVR_ROUTER_USE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_router_use \- append middleware to a sub-router
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_router_use(chttpsvr_router *router,
                                   chttpsvr_middleware_fn fn, void *ctx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends middleware to the given sub-router's chain.  This middleware
runs after global middleware and before the route handler, but only
for requests routed through this sub-router.

This function is thread-safe and may be called before or after
chttpsvr_start is running.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
See the NOTES section of chttpsvr_use for the per-router
registration-time cap, the combined dispatch-time middleware limit (32
steps per request), and the first-wins duplicate-route policy.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args if router or fn is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory if allocation fails.
ccol_not_permitted if this router's middleware chain is already at the
32-entry cap.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_use (3),
.BR chttpsvr_subrouter (3)
